      ":question/id": "0c24f864-598b-5f81-946b-8069e63f6b70",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-2-(2)xy?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(0,-2)$,$(3,-1)$,$(1,3)$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,-2)}=-2-2(0)(-2)=-2, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(3,-1)}=-2-2(3)(-1)=4, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,3)}=-2-2(1)(3)=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/2b/2bdcf56e6a7c6918ccee32f76363ad7c3096d213bd6ebc885040f78f2e7b8b10.png)",
